Before opening the browser, I recommend these three checks:

cat conf/tomcat-users.xml | tail -10

You should see:

<role rolename="manager-gui"/>
<role rolename="manager-script"/>
<user username="tomcat" password="admin@123" roles="manager-gui,manager-script"/>
</tomcat-users>

Then:

grep -n "RemoteCIDRValve" webapps/manager/META-INF/context.xml

It should return nothing.

Then:

ss -lntp | grep 8080

You should see Tomcat listening on:

:8080

Then open:

http://YOUR-EC2-PUBLIC-IP:8080

and Manager:

http://YOUR-EC2-PUBLIC-IP:8080/manager/html

Credentials:

Username: tomcat
Password: admin@123
